WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.510
Sometimes, the SCP Foundation needs to get
creative with how they go about securing,

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.410
containing, and protecting.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:12.670
Sadly not everything can be solved with a
Mobile Task Force, or by locking it away securely

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:14.660
in a concrete chamber.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:21.630
Which brings us to SCP-2480, otherwise known
by the nickname “An Unfinished Ritual.”

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:26.589
When initially looking through the file on
SCP-2480, the reader will immediately notice

00:00:26.589 --> 00:00:29.179
a number of discrepancies throughout.

00:00:29.179 --> 00:00:30.960
Parts of the entry have been crossed out.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.420
They’ve been struck through so they are
still readable, not redacted completely for

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:40.359
the purposes of secrecy like many of the details
in other SCP files.

00:00:40.359 --> 00:00:46.879
First and foremost, SCP-2480 has been reclassified
multiple times, first as “Safe”, then

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:49.489
changed to the infamous “Keter” class.

00:00:49.489 --> 00:00:54.050
But now, it is listed as the far more ominous
“Presumed Neutralized.”

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:59.379
It’s disconcerting, because “presumed”
definitely leaves a lot of questions.

00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:03.230
So, what exactly is SCP-2480?

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:10.070
SCP-2480 is an area of dimensional abnormality,
apparently created when an occult ritual was

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:16.250
interrupted in November of 1952, hence the
nickname of “An Unfinished Ritual.”

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.520
The source of this anomaly is located in a
heavily forested town somewhere near the coast

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.080
of Massachusetts.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.920
Of course, this state has long been synonymous
with many occult happenings, Massachusetts

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:33.110
famously being home to a number of supposedly
haunted houses and sites of supernatural activity.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:39.640
And SCP-2480 is no exception, seeming to fit
both of those criteria.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:46.090
In order to keep an eye on SCP-2480, the Foundation
has dispatched Mobile Task Force Epsilon-6,

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.720
also codenamed the “Village Idiots.”

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.450
These operatives are working undercover in
the surrounding area and nearby town, keeping

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.430
watch for any sightings of anomalous activity.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:02.680
Meanwhile, another team, MTF Psi-9 the “Abyss
Gazers”, are stationed nearby, in case any

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.570
incidents should arise.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:09.060
These operatives have been authorized by the
SCP Foundation to employ the use of lethal

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.750
force on any and all anomalous manifestations
they should encounter.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:17.040
Their directive is to destroy without prejudice.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.040
That sure sounds like a lot of effort to secure
something classed as “Presumed Neutralized”.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:27.620
The anomaly itself is centered around an old
Massachusetts house, known as Bodfel Manor.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.790
The manor was once the home of a millionaire
industrialist by the name of Cornelius P.

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:36.340
Bodfel III, who died in 1952 at the age of
eighty-six.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:42.920
And yes, he died in the same year that the
ritual that created SCP-2480 took place.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:46.550
But we’re sure that’s probably just a
coincidence, right?

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:51.370
Interestingly, during his life, Cornelius
Bodfel apparently had something of a fascination

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:52.510
with the occult.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:57.750
It was likely this interest that drew him
to creating a supernatural cult known as Adytum’s

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:58.750
Wake.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:03.270
Little is known about this organization and
Adytum’s Wake are not part of the SCP Foundation’s

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:08.680
Groups of Interest, the list of other anomalous
groups that often rival the Foundation.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:12.459
Much like the anomaly itself, they’re presumed
neutralized.

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:17.260
The Foundation conducted a full scale investigation
into Bodfel Manor, and were able to unearth

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:20.040
more information about the aforementioned
cult.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:25.291
Fortunately, Cornelius Bodfel kept a series
of meticulous and detailed journals, as well

00:03:25.291 --> 00:03:30.280
as photographs that give plenty of insight
into the activities of Adytum’s Wake.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:34.500
Unfortunately, a lot of what they got up to
wasn’t all that pleasant.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.700
But what did you expect from a group of cultists?

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:42.520
Adytum’s Wake would engage in all kinds
of depraved behavior, some that’s better

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.330
left to the imagination.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:49.510
What we can say is they’d often perform
ritualistic human sacrifice and indulge in

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:53.550
cannibalism, and these are some of their less
unpleasant crimes.

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:58.300
On site personnel also uncovered sermon notes
in Bodfel’s journals, detailing the cult’s

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.120
services and occult practices.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:05.180
They also found lists of the Adytum’s Wake
members, including local wealthy families

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:11.150
and respected politicians, other industrialists
like Cornelius Bodfel, and even priests and

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.819
other religious figures.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:16.819
The Foundation had previously been aware of
Adytum’s Wake, but initially dismissed the

00:04:16.819 --> 00:04:22.449
group as little more than a “decadent upper-class
social club” not worthy of a full investigation.

00:04:22.449 --> 00:04:24.280
Let’s review, shall we?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:29.550
We have a dimensional anomaly in a Massachusetts
manor, a cult obsessed with the supernatural,

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:36.979
and some sort of ritual that occurred in November,
1952, but was interrupted before its completion.

00:04:36.979 --> 00:04:41.539
All parts of the same bizarre and twisted
puzzle, but there’s still a piece yet to

00:04:41.539 --> 00:04:42.789
be uncovered.

00:04:42.789 --> 00:04:44.029
That missing piece?

00:04:44.029 --> 00:04:46.199
The Global Occult Coalition.

00:04:46.199 --> 00:04:50.470
Who would have expected the GOC to rear their
ugly heads around here?

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:54.740
Though it’s worth mentioning that many of
the GOC’s member groups are occult in nature,

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:58.650
so it probably shouldn’t come as that much
of a surprise that they were somehow involved

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.400
in this case, too..

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.800
It goes without saying that the SCP Foundation
shares a complicated relationship with this

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.699
particular Group of Interest, each often disagreeing
with the other’s methods.

00:05:09.699 --> 00:05:15.330
Occasionally, the GOC and SCP Foundation will
put aside their differences and act as allies

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:20.199
against large scale threats like The Scarlet
King, but any alliance between them is often

00:05:20.199 --> 00:05:22.680
uneasy and short lived.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:27.590
In the case of SCP-2480, The Foundation were
first alerted to the anomaly’s existence

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:32.560
when they decoded a GOC distress signal, tracing
its source to Bodfel Manor.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:36.659
When the investigative team arrived, they
found deceased bodies littered throughout

00:05:36.659 --> 00:05:39.770
the estate, thirty six corpses in total.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:43.749
Eight of these were confirmed to be Coalition
operatives and the rest were theorized to

00:05:43.749 --> 00:05:46.099
be dead members of Adytum’s Wake.

00:05:46.099 --> 00:05:50.129
Almost all of the corpses found at Bodfel
Manor displayed signs of anomalous causes

00:05:50.129 --> 00:05:56.229
of death - some had imploded, some disintegrated,
and others had their bodies twisted into fatal

00:05:56.229 --> 00:05:57.280
new shapes.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:02.550
At first glance, and given the GOC’s mission
to destroy the supernatural, it looked as

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.569
if they had stormed in and interrupted the
Adytum’s Wake cult while they were right

00:06:06.569 --> 00:06:08.699
in the middle of performing a ritual.

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:16.379
Things went awry, SCP-2480 was created, and
caused everyone nearby to die horrifically.

00:06:16.379 --> 00:06:18.370
Surely that’s the whole story, right?

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.860
Well, not quite, as it turns out.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:26.009
While there were no surviving GOC operatives
for the Foundation to interrogate, the investigative

00:06:26.009 --> 00:06:31.069
team were able to uncover documents related
to the operation in a nearby safehouse used

00:06:31.069 --> 00:06:32.610
by the GOC.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:37.430
Much of the official documentation was destroyed
in an attempted coverup, but a torn remainder

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.819
of a mission report was recovered in the safehouse’s
fireplace.

00:06:40.819 --> 00:06:45.969
It was actually the Global Occult Coalition
who had initiated the ritual, though its true

00:06:45.969 --> 00:06:47.719
purpose was lost.

00:06:47.719 --> 00:06:52.770
The Foundation had learned that the SCP-2480
area had been inadvertently created by the

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:56.509
GOC and their heavy-handed approach to their
mission.

00:06:56.509 --> 00:07:01.110
But why would an anti-occult organization
attempt a supernatural ritual?

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:05.770
Theories as to their intention seem to point
to the penultimate piece of the puzzle: Sarkicism,

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:10.039
a widespread religious cult that worships
flesh and disease.

00:07:10.039 --> 00:07:14.689
The very existence of this religion is viewed
as a threat of apocalyptic proportions by

00:07:14.689 --> 00:07:16.789
the SCP Foundation.

00:07:16.789 --> 00:07:21.789
Sarkicism was initially founded by the Grand
Karcist Ion, but it has since split into a

00:07:21.789 --> 00:07:24.559
number of smaller sub-groups over the millennia.

00:07:24.559 --> 00:07:26.249
And among those groups?

00:07:26.249 --> 00:07:27.330
Adytum’s Wake.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:32.059
The GOC mission report fragment gathered by
the Foundation describes the operatives’

00:07:32.059 --> 00:07:34.869
target to be Grand Karcist Ion himself.

00:07:34.869 --> 00:07:40.310
He apparently cannot be directly perceived,
so few actual descriptions of his form exist.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:44.970
It has been noted, by some, to be humanoid
in appearance at least, wearing what looks

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:49.059
to be vestments similar to a priest’s and
carrying a staff.

00:07:49.059 --> 00:07:54.699
Ion is able to disappear and reappear at will,
and possesses a plethora of reality-altering

00:07:54.699 --> 00:07:55.779
capabilities.

00:07:55.779 --> 00:08:00.999
The Sarkic founder is able to shift and reshape
any organic material, as well as having the

00:08:00.999 --> 00:08:04.580
ability to bend the very fabric of reality
around him.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:11.610
While he may hold a humanoid shape, this entity
is certainly not human, at least not any longer.

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:16.729
Functionally immortal, Grand Karcist Ion is
noted to frequently exhibit signs of malignant

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:18.710
narcissism and megalomania.

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:25.839
So, now the story shifts: The GOC was attempting
to use Adytum’s Wake to summon Ion in order

00:08:25.839 --> 00:08:29.179
for them to eradicate the leader of the Sarkic
religion.

00:08:29.179 --> 00:08:35.229
The plan backfired though, SCP-2480 was summoned,
and both the cult and Coalition operatives

00:08:35.229 --> 00:08:36.229
were killed.

00:08:36.229 --> 00:08:38.339
End of story, right?

00:08:38.339 --> 00:08:42.019
Except there is one more twist in this tale
of cults and secrets.

00:08:42.019 --> 00:08:45.940
And that twist came from the last place anyone
would expect…

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:50.050
It came from inside the SCP Foundation.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:56.190
After SCP-2480 was created by the ritual at
Bodfel Manor, Site 13 was established in order

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:58.089
to keep the anomalous area contained.

00:08:58.089 --> 00:09:03.960
You see, if the ritual was an atomic blast,
then SCP-2480 was both the crater and the

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.709
nuclear fallout from that blast.

00:09:06.709 --> 00:09:11.590
Except instead of causing radiation sickness,
the entire area around Bodfel Manor became

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:16.339
dimensionally unstable and prone to anomalous
occurrences.

00:09:16.339 --> 00:09:21.120
Overseeing Site 13 was Director Simon Oswalt,
a Foundation bureaucrat.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.790
Simon had been selected for this duty thanks
to his distinct lack of imagination, and because

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:31.440
the anomalous area of SCP-2480 was thought
to be inconsequential at the time.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:37.560
In 1988, Oswalt failed to deliver his regular
report on SCP-2480’s activity.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:41.170
This was initially thought to be a simple
error, except the Foundation couldn’t get

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:43.370
in contact with Site 13.

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:44.410
Why?

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:47.720
Because the Unfinished Ritual hadn’t actually
failed.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:53.279
It wasn’t unfinished, the GOC had succeeded
in summoning Grand Karcist Ion.

00:09:53.279 --> 00:09:57.320
And Simon Oswalt had been the one to discover
this.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:02.139
The founder of Sarkicism appeared to Oswalt,
who was converted and turned against his superiors

00:10:02.139 --> 00:10:03.850
at the SCP Foundation.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:09.279
Ion was able to exert his influence over the
former bureaucrat, swaying him to change sides

00:10:09.279 --> 00:10:14.240
by showing Oswalt a description in the Foundation’s
personnel dossier on him that referred to

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.449
him as a “mirthless dullard.”

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:21.370
Turning his back on the Foundation and pledging
himself to Sarkicism, Simon Oswalt was granted

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:24.379
anomalous abilities by Grand Karcist Ion.

00:10:24.379 --> 00:10:29.259
Oswalt was given the power to control an army
of anomalous entities called Sarkites that

00:10:29.259 --> 00:10:33.230
he could summon through the area of SCP-2480.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:38.670
Grand Karcist Ion dubbed Simon with a new
name, Karcist Karvas, and made him the leader

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.389
of his new army.

00:10:40.389 --> 00:10:46.060
Their goal was to bring about the Sarkic religion’s
ideal, the dawn of a new age of flesh that

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:48.810
would spell destruction for humanity.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:53.860
When the Foundation lost contact with Site
13, they dispatched two agents to investigate,

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:56.250
Samuel Roe and Sarah Valentine.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:11:01.449
Unaware of Oswalt’s conversion to Sarkicism
and his new purpose as Karcist Karvas, both

00:11:01.449 --> 00:11:05.400
agents were captured by the Sarkite creatures
within SCP-2480.

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:11.379
The same monsters were also terrorizing the
nearby town, replacing citizens and sometimes

00:11:11.379 --> 00:11:14.270
even kidnapping and devouring them.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:19.060
Another team was later sent in to survey the
area, only to be killed or replaced as well,

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:22.820
with only one survivor: Doctor Calixto Narváez.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:27.209
Narváez reported on the situation to the
O5 Council, and in collaboration with the

00:11:27.209 --> 00:11:31.810
Global Occult Coalition, the Foundation launched
an assault against Oswalt.

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:36.810
The joint task force of the two organizations
were able to neutralize the Sarkites, reclaiming

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:41.170
the area of SCP-2480 and capturing Simon Oswalt.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:46.120
Without his control, the creatures became
directionless, unable to so much as eat or

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.600
defend themselves.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:53.250
Grand Karcist Ion’s plan had been thwarted,
and Oswalt was taken back to an SCP Foundation

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:57.649
Site, though now under a new name: SCP-2480-1.

00:11:57.649 --> 00:12:03.389
However, during an operation at Containment
Area 14, Oswalt seemed to suffer no effects

00:12:03.389 --> 00:12:05.959
from anaesthetic or surgical incision.

00:12:05.959 --> 00:12:10.649
Foundation researchers were horrified to learn
that Oswalt no longer possessed any internal

00:12:10.649 --> 00:12:14.470
organs, save for his brain, heart, and lungs.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:15.889
The rest of him was empty.

00:12:15.889 --> 00:12:21.019
Later, he was interrogated and began raving
about Grand Karcist Ion, so much that the

00:12:21.019 --> 00:12:24.420
doctor questioning Oswalt attempted to attack
him.

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:29.120
Breaking free of his restraints, Simon Oswalt
amputated both of the doctor’s arms before

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.680
he was re-contained by guards.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:37.569
Since then, the area of SCP-2480 has been
mostly quiet, but it still remains under the

00:12:37.569 --> 00:12:42.830
Foundation’s close watch just in case any
anomalous happenings start up again.

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:47.290
But if you’re planning a tour of the many
haunted old houses of Massachusetts, we’d

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:51.110
recommend maybe avoiding Bodfel Manor, just
to be safe.

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:57.839
Now go check out “SCP-1730 - What Happened
to Site-13?” and “SCP-4999 - Someone to

00:12:57.839 --> 00:13:02.330
Watch Over Us Tale” for more supernatural
tales from the SCP Foundation!

